s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jobfynder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jobfynder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created":false,"deleted":false,"base_ref":null,"compare":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/compare/db5df748f7bf...41155a9f0c55","commits":[{"id":"82a781fe0b6810ece22a991449f68ad85e1b60d6","tree_id":"30be3c5af8bf3f1953b17336e3d2133db1f357b6","distinct":false,"message":"Dashboard redesign + review queues that actually clear\n\nWhy the queues never cleared: the 15-minute triage only decided cases it was\ncertain about and left everything else \"for review\" forever. The ~6,200\nboilerplate lines in the queue were almost all real job requirements repeated\nby many vendors (same job reposted), and the skills were mostly phrases,\nheadings and bullet artefacts.\n\n* triage_rules.py: shared second-tier rules. Rejects non-skills / job content\n  (conservative: rejecting never strips or adds anything); approves only\n  distinctive product-name signals; every verdict carries a plain-English\n  reason. Triage runner uses it (policy hermes-auto-v3 re-evaluates the\n  backlog once).\n* GET /taxonomy-candidates returns suggestion + reason per row.\n* GET /drafts/review/today (workbench.py): health checks, what needs a human,\n  what Hermes did, pipeline funnel. Best-effort per section, 45s cache.\n* get_pipeline_stats: one table scan instead of seven (was timing out).\n* Frontend: left-nav layout, new Today home, new Review queue (tabs for\n  skills / titles / repeated lines, \"needs your decision\" lens, apply\n  suggestions) with the sender blocklist moved to the bottom.\n* Tests: triage rules, route-policy entry; fix flaky dedup test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-11-09T10:25:04-05:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/82a781fe0b6810ece22a991449f68ad85e1b60d6","author":{"name":"Jobfynder","email":"167116843+